# Widget Configuration

See [README Widget configuration](../../README.md#widget-configuration).

## Best practices

- Define `callbackTable` and `styleSheet` at **mount time** (in `mountWidget`, `render*.ts`, or `App.tsx`), not inline on `segFactory` / `cardFactory`.
- `callbackTable` keys are `typeName` values from preprocessor-generated `GenEntities` (globally unique across segments and cards).
- `styleSheet` keys are segment `typeName` values from `GenSegments`.
- When a `callbackTable` entry exists for a type + event, it **overrides** any inline mouse handler on the factory. Otherwise the inline handler is used.

## Example mount pattern

```typescript
mountWidget({
  host,
  vertical,
  horizontal,
  card,
  styleSheet: createPeriodicTableStyleSheet(),
  callbackTable: createPeriodicTableCallbackTable({ elementSelect }),
});
```

Keep domain factories free of inline mouse handlers and `style` when the example provides view-level `callbackTable` / `styleSheet` modules. Layout-only examples (e.g. timetable) may pass `styleSheet` alone and omit `callbackTable`.

Do **not** store `CardVi` or `SegVi` in application or example code. Widget owns those trees; look up `card.vis[treeUuid]` at the call site. See [CardVi and SegVi](../../README.md#cardvi-and-segvi) and [cardvi-segvi.mdc](cardvi-segvi.mdc).
